  "reason": "The current best (config_039, 0.725) uses scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted in the multiprofile setting. All 7 completed experiments are multiprofile, so the singleprofile dimension is completely unexplored. config_007 tests whether a single profile (no aggregation step) with the best-known encoders (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l) and weighted fusion can match or exceed the multiprofile result. This is critical because: (1) it reduces model complexity and training cost (no transformer aggregation), (2) it clarifies whether the multiprofile aggregation is genuinely adding signal or just adding parameters, and (3) if it matches the current best at lower cost, it frees GPU budget for the final 2 experiments to explore other directions. Expected cost: ~2.5–3.0 GPU hours (cheaper than config_039's 3.60 since there is no multiprofile transformer aggregation). This is the highest-information experiment remaining: it either confirms multiprofile is necessary or reveals a simpler, cheaper path to comparable accuracy."
